from the intriguing and mysterious plot  the soundtrack boozing with 80s bangers  and Winona Ryder's incredible turn as  Joyce buyers there's a lot to love about  the new Netflix original series stranger  things for my money it does an excellent  job of referencing cult 80 sci-fi  without it becoming completely  overbearing if you like stranger things  and are looking for something with a  similar flavor here's a few of its key  influences these are all well worth  checking out if you haven't seen or read  them already but if you haven't seen the  show then don't worry  spoilers are gonna be kept to an  absolute minimum because you seriously  need to delve into that mystery as fresh  as possible let's kick off with a fairly  obvious one as the show is basically a  giant omage to Stephen King's work even  down to the logo so naturally Steve is  absolutely loving it King excels in  telling stories about the ordinary  meeting the extraordinary usually  involving small town locals coming up  against improbable and surreal  situations not unlike the citizens of  Hawking's Indiana who get embroiled in a  missing-child case come up against  psychic powers a sinister government  agency and some kind of world ending  evil but with so many King books to read  which of his novels have influenced  stranger things the most well the misfit  bullied kids who seem to be targeted by  a powerful otherworldly enemy is taken  right out of it yes this is the one with  the terrifying clown monster but it's  also a story about friendship and  adorable kids working together to take  on the ultimate evil stranger things  really kicks off when some dark entity  escapes from the halkans National  Laboratory and out into the town this  motif has been explored in multiple King  novels such as the stand which in my  opinion is his magnum opus  it's where the US Army scientists create  a weaponized strain of flu only to be  completely unprepared for when it  inevitably escapes destroying something  like 99% of the world's population the  character of L in the show is a direct  parallel to Charlie McGee from the novel  firestarter both a young girls with  unnatural psychic powers but where L  lived a life of captivity  and was experimented upon at the Hawkins  National Lab Charlie's powers were a  result of government experimentation on  her parents her family ends up on the  run from a government agency known as  the shop who are determined to track  Charlie down to use her powers as a  weapon  just like Elle you could also compare  Elle to Carrie White from Kings first  novel Carrie which also follows a young  girl as she struggles to come to terms  with her new psychic powers all the  Stephen King books I just talked about  have film adaptations of varying degrees  of quality I'd maybe give firestarter  and the 2013 Carrie remake a Miss but  there are other movies that have really  inspired stranger things there's a lot  of spielberg in there like ET the  extra-terrestrial following kids who  befriend a strange and mysterious alien  while trying to keep it hidden from  grownups and of course the government  who just want to run experiments on it  whereas in the show it's Mike and his  friends trying to keep L safe  there's also Close Encounters of the  Third Kind an average guy has a close  encounter but no one believes him very  similar to how no one believes all the  weird stuff that Joyce and Hopper  discover and think that they've gone a  little bit crazy instead and if you like  the motif of nerdy kids banding together  to solve crimes and uncover mysteries  and go on adventures together there is  of course the Goonies and Stand By Me  The Goonies features loads of typical  80s character stereotypes the gang of  misfit kids the outcasts older brother  the sensible salt of the earth best  friends all of who we can see in some  form or another in stranger things in  Stand By Me which is also an adaptation  of a Stephen King novella boy did the  stranger things guys love Stephen King  there's a strong friendship group made  up of four boys you go on one last  adventure together to try and find the  body of a missing boy they tell each  other stories and jokes and have a  special handshake and are basically the  strong friendship group who go through  ups and downs together just like Mike  Lukas dust in and of course will do and  of course this cult TV shows that have a  huge influence on stranger things like  The Twilight Zone and the short-lived  Outer Limits who are both filled with  lingering dread  Bend's and psychological horror we are  controlling transmission if we wish to  make it louder  we will bring up the button  if we wish to make it softer we will  tune it to a whisper all of which  stranger things has in spades Twin Peaks  is another there's plenty of parallels  to draw  Special Agent Dale Cooper investigates  the murder of homecoming queen Laura  Palmer is small in Sela town similarly  chief hopper gets dragged into a series  of mysteries in a small insular town  that all begin with young will fires  going missing so there's a few cult  inspirations for stranger things I'm  sure to have missed some I mean there  was loads to choose from so let me know  your favorites in the comments below for  more on strange things make sure you  like the video and subscribe to  youtube.com / GameSpot and we will see  you next time  you
 

